d2d1: Draw lines without building a path geometry.

DrawLine() created a path geometry for every line, with a sink, a figure,
its vertex and segment arrays, Close(), and the outline, then released
all of it. Affinity draws its ruler ticks with DrawLine(), tens of
thousands a second while the canvas redraws.

Build the line's outline directly instead, the four vertices and two
triangles d2d_geometry_add_figure_outline() makes for a single open
segment, and draw them as DrawGeometry() would (identity geometry
transform, the same stroke width handling; stroke styles are ignored as
before). Command lists still record the line.

The d2d1 conformance tests give the same result before and after (17491
tests, 0 failures); Affinity's rulers render identically. Brush tip
behind the cursor, on top of 0058, OpenCL on, 18 strokes each: median
30 -> 26 ms.

